R"VG(
# futuristic10.vg (H-04's second pass): a life's events as the archive's writer tells them (`@life ar.life n`: the person's own events
# that have a rule here): the marriage, the children, the moves; the public things they did (a deed, an invention, a work, a contest, a
# trial, a play, an embassy); and the family's everyday the history keeps (an illness, an injury, an apprenticeship, a house built or
# burnt, a quarrel, a journey, a betrothal).

ar.life.marriage
  ($e.b.person!=1) I married {$e.b:name} in the {#$e.year:ord} year of {city}, at {$e.place}. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person=1) {$e.a:name} and I were married at {$e.place}, a long time ago now. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person!=1) I married {$e.b:name} at {$e.place} under {skyone}, with {food} for everyone and too little {drink}. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person!=1) {$e.b:name} and I were married at {$e.place} in the old way, with {feast.custom}. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person!=1) I met {$e.b:name} at {feast.custom} and married {$e.b:obj} at {$e.place} within the year. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person!=1) In my {#$me.age:ord} year I married {$e.b:name}; {ar.wedding}. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person=1) {$e.a:name} asked me, and I said yes before the question was finished. We married at {$e.place}. {ar.after}
ar.wedding
  the children carried {colour.holy} lamps
  it rained, and that is supposed to be lucky
  the machines played the wrong music and nobody minded
  my mother cried through all of it
  we swore {oath}, which is the old oath
  {instrument} played until the neighbours complained
ar.life.birth
  ($e.a.gender=she) My daughter {$e.a:name} was born at {$e.place}. {ar.after}
  ($e.a.gender=he) My son {$e.a:name} was born at {$e.place}. {ar.after}
  ($e.a.gender=she) {$e.a:name}, my daughter, came {fut.when.past}, at {$e.place}. {ar.after}
  ($e.a.gender=he) {$e.a:name}, my son, came {fut.when.past}, at {$e.place}. {ar.after}
  ($e.a.gender=she) Our daughter {$e.a:name} was born in the {#$e.year:ord} year of {city}; we called her {endear}. {ar.after}
  ($e.a.gender=he) Our son {$e.a:name} was born in the {#$e.year:ord} year of {city}; we called him {endear}. {ar.after}
ar.life.move
  We moved to {$e.place2} when {ar.why}. {ar.after}
  In the {#$e.year:ord} year I left {$e.place} for {$e.place2}, because {ar.why}. {ar.after}
  I went to live at {$e.place2}; {ar.why2}. {ar.after}
ar.life.betrothal
  ($e.b.person!=1) In the {#$e.year:ord} year I was promised to {$e.b:name}. We had met twice. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person!=1) I was promised to {$e.b:name} at {$e.place} over a bowl of {food}, before either of us had much say in it. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person=1) I was promised to {$e.a:name} at {$e.place}. Our mothers had settled it over {drink}. {ar.after}
  ($e.b.person!=1) {$e.b:name} and I were promised at {feast.custom}, with {#n|witness} and {food} for everyone. {ar.after}
ar.life.apprentice
  At {$e.place} I was put to a {$e.what} to learn the trade. {ar.trade} {ar.after}
  I was apprenticed to a {$e.what} at {$e.place} when I was small. {ar.trade} {ar.after}
  In the {#$e.year:ord} year my mother took me to a {$e.what} at {$e.place} and left me there, with my things in {vessel.one}. {ar.trade}
  I learned the trade of a {$e.what} at {$e.place}, mostly by watching and being shouted at. {ar.trade}
ar.trade (share=0.8)
  The {craft} was harder than it looked, and it looked hard.
  I made my master {food} for a year before I was allowed near the work.
  On my first {festival} there I was given a {colour.holy} cord, which apprentices wore then.
  I swept for a year before I was allowed to touch anything.
  The first thing I made, I still have; it is terrible.
  My master said I had good hands and no patience. Half of that was true.
  I learned more from the other apprentices than from the master.
ar.life.house
  We had the house at {$e.place} from the {#$e.year:ord} year. {ar.houseline} {ar.after}
  ($e.what=built) We built our own house at {$e.place}, {walls.of>.w} on {.w}, and it is still standing. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=bought) We bought the house at {$e.place} from a family that was leaving. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=sold) We sold the old house at {$e.place}. I walk past it sometimes. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=burnt) Our house at {$e.place} burned. We got the children out and nothing else. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=flooded) The water came into our house at {$e.place}; we lived upstairs for a season. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=mended) We mended the house at {$e.place} ourselves, badly, and it held. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=room) We built a room onto the house at {$e.place}, for a child who had not been born yet. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=roof) We put a new roof on the house at {$e.place}: {roofs}, the old kind. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=moved) We moved house within {$e.place}, three streets, with everything on our backs. {ar.after}
ar.houseline (share=0.8)
  It had {roofs} and a door with {motif.over}, and it leaked in {weather}.
  The {herd} lived under it in the cold months, which kept us warm and kept us awake.
  My father carved {motif.over} over the door himself, badly; I would not change them.
  It is still there, though someone else's {beast} sleeps on the step now.
ar.life.illness
  ($e.what=fever) I had a fever at {$e.place} that nearly took me. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what=cough) I had a cough at {$e.place} that lasted a whole season. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what=spots|$e.what=headaches|$e.what=earache|$e.what=toothache) I had {$e.what} at {$e.place}, for longer than I like to remember. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what=flux) I had the flux at {$e.place}. We will not go into it. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what=chill) I caught a chill at {$e.place} and kept it all season. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what=rash) I had a rash at {$e.place} that the doctors could not name. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what!=fever $e.what!=cough $e.what!=spots $e.what!=headaches $e.what!=earache $e.what!=toothache $e.what!=flux $e.what!=chill $e.what!=rash) {$e.what}, the doctors called it: it kept me in bed at {$e.place} for {#n|week}. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what!=fever $e.what!=cough $e.what!=spots $e.what!=headaches $e.what!=earache $e.what!=toothache $e.what!=flux $e.what!=chill $e.what!=rash) I was in bed at {$e.place} for {#n|week} with what the doctors called {$e.what}. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what=fever|$e.what=cough|$e.what=chill|$e.what=rash) In the {#$e.year:ord} year I was ill at {$e.place}: a {$e.what}, nothing more, they said. {ar.ill}
  ($e.what=fever|$e.what=cough|$e.what=flux|$e.what=chill|$e.what=rash|$e.what=spots|$e.what=headaches|$e.what=earache|$e.what=toothache) The year of my {$e.what}, my children call it, the year at {$e.place}. {ar.ill}
ar.ill (share=0.8)
  My mother sat up with me every night of it.
  The {craft} workshop sent me work to do in bed, so I would not go mad.
  They brought me {food} and I could not eat it, which frightened everyone.
  I was given the old remedy, {~remedy}, and swore {oath} that I would never take it again.
  The machines watched me all night; I could hear them deciding not to worry.
  A {beast} slept on my feet the whole time and would not be moved.
  I lay listening to {instrument} from the {fut.common} and got better out of spite.
  I got better, which was not what anyone expected.
  It left me with a cough I still have when {weather} comes.
  They gave me {drink} and {food}, and the old remedies, and one of them worked.
  I read every record in the archive while I lay there.
ar.life.injury
  I hurt my {$e.what} at {$e.place}, {ar.inj}. {ar.after}
  At {$e.place} I hurt my {$e.what} and could not work for a season. {ar.after}
  In the {#$e.year:ord} year I broke something in my {$e.what} at {$e.place}; the machines mended it and I have complained about it ever since. {ar.after}
  My {$e.what} has never been right since a day at {$e.place}, {ar.inj}. {ar.after}
ar.inj (share=0.8)
  falling off the long stair
  in the {herd} pens, which the {herd} found funny
  at {festival}, which is no excuse
  practising {craft} too late at night
  in the {fut.green}, of all places
  showing off
  carrying {vessel} that were too heavy for me
  at {pastime}
  doing nothing at all, which is the worst way
ar.life.quarrel
  In the {#$e.year:ord} year I fell out with half of {$e.place} over {ar.qwhat}. {ar.after}
  (has:$e.b) I quarrelled with {$e.b:name} over {ar.qwhat}, at {$e.place}. We made it up eventually, mostly. {ar.after}
  (has:$e.b) {$e.b:name} and I did not speak for a year over {ar.qwhat}. It was my fault. Do not tell {$e.b:obj}. {ar.after}
  (!has:$e.b) There was a quarrel at {$e.place} over {ar.qwhat}, and I was in the middle of it. {ar.after}
ar.qwhat
  ($e.what=wall) a wall
  ($e.what=water) the water
  ($e.what=debt) a debt
  ($e.what=inheritance) an inheritance
  ($e.what=dog) a dog
  ($e.what=boundary) a boundary
  ($e.what=marriage) a marriage
  ($e.what=tree) a tree
  ($e.what=noise) the noise
  ($e.what=path) a path
  ($e.what=beasts) the {herd}
  ($e.what=loan) a loan
ar.life.journey
  I went to {$e.place2} {ar.jwhy}. {ar.after}
  Once I travelled to {$e.place2} {ar.jwhy}; it took {#n|day}, and I talked to everyone. {ar.after}
  I went to {$e.place2} {ar.jwhy} and brought back {food} nobody at home would eat. {ar.after}
  In the {#$e.year:ord} year I travelled to {$e.place2} {ar.jwhy}, and came back changed, a little. {ar.after}
ar.jwhy
  ($e.what=trade) to trade
  ($e.what=kin) to see my kin
  ($e.what=pilgrimage) on pilgrimage
  ($e.what=work) for work
  ($e.what=fair) for the fair
  ($e.what=study) to study
  ($e.what=law) about a lawsuit
  ($e.what=wedding) for a wedding
  ($e.what=funeral) for a funeral
  ($e.what=doctor) to see a doctor

ar.life.deed
  ($e.deed=song) I made a song that people still sing, which I did not expect. {ar.after}
  ($e.deed=book) I wrote a book. Everyone read it once, and then they had read it. {ar.after}
  ($e.deed=taught) I taught at {$e.place} for most of my life. {ar.after}
  ($e.deed=healed) I was a healer at {$e.place}, in a bad time. {ar.after}
  ($e.deed=gardens) I made the gardens at {$e.place}. Go and sit in them. {ar.after}
  ($e.deed=pictures) I made the moving pictures they still show at {festival}. {ar.after}
  ($e.deed=theory) I had an idea about the world that turned out to be true, mostly. {ar.after}
  ($e.deed=map) I drew the map they use now. {ar.after}
  I did a thing at {$e.place} that the archive calls a deed. It felt like work. {ar.after}
ar.life.invention
  I made {$e.invention}, at {$e.place}; it was not as clever as people say. {ar.after}
  At {$e.place} I worked out {$e.invention}. My teachers said it could not be done, which helped. {ar.after}
ar.life.built
  I helped build {$e.work} at {$e.place}. It took {#$e.value|year}. {ar.after}
  {$e.work} at {$e.place} is partly mine. I laid the floor of the east side. {ar.after}
ar.life.discovery
  I went where nobody had gone, and came back to {$e.place}. {ar.after}
ar.life.games
  I won at the games at {$e.place} once, the year everyone else was ill. {ar.after}
  At {$e.place} I won the games, at {$e.what}. I still have the {colour.holy} ribbon. {ar.after}
ar.life.trial
  ($e.verdict=acquitted) I was tried at {$e.place} for {$e.what} and found not guilty, which I was. {ar.after}
  ($e.verdict!=acquitted) I was tried at {$e.place} for {$e.what}. I will not say more than the archive does. {ar.after}
ar.life.show
  ($e.what=play) My play was first given at {$e.place}. {#n|person} walked out; the rest stayed. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=song) My song was first sung at {$e.place}, by somebody better than me. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=film) My film was first shown at {$e.place}. I was too frightened to watch it. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=poem) My poem was first read at {$e.place}, too fast. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=pictures) My pictures were first shown at {$e.place}. People stood in front of them for a long time, or politely. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=statue) My statue was set up at {$e.place}. The {bird} found it first. {ar.after}
  ($e.what=dance) My dance was first danced at {$e.place}, and I danced in it, once. {ar.after}
ar.life.embassy
  I went as an envoy for {$e.place}. Mostly it was waiting in rooms. {ar.after}
ar.life.institution
  I helped found {$e.instname}. It outlasted my interest in it. {ar.after}
ar.life.faith
  I preached at {$e.place}, once, and some of them listened. {ar.after}
ar.life.none
  Nothing much happened to me, except {feast.custom} every year, which I have come to think of as a kind of luck.
  I never married and never moved. I have been here among the {herd} the whole time, and I liked it.
  My life was ordinary from one end to the other, like {crop} bread, and I would not trade it.
  I kept {craft} going when nobody else would. That is my whole story, and enough.
  I did my work, I kept {festival}, I fed the {herd}. Nobody will make a song of it on {instrument}.
)VG"
